Token Bucket Algo **********

Amazon, stripe use this for rate limiting their api requests

                    Refiller (to fill the bucket)
Requests        Bucket(having some capacity, 2 req/s)
                    |
condition if we have enough tokens?
if yes then we process the req and reduce the capacity

if no then drop the request

what all we need?
-bucket size 
-refill rate

now our app can have different use cases , so for different scenarios we need different buckets

eg
1 bucket we can only do 10 posts per sec
1 bucket for we can make 150 friends per day
1 bucket we can like only 500 posts per day

so we need 3 buckets

if we based on ip address rate limit then req 1 bucket
on base of user id then also 1 bucket req


Benefits?
- it i easy to implement
- it is memory efficient
- lesser breaches or bucket leaks

cons: it has two params so it is bit hard to 'Tune'



Leaky Bucket Algo **********

similar to token bucket almost


                    Refiller (to fill the bucket)
Requests        Bucket(having some capacity, 100 req/s)
                    |
                  if bucket/queue is full drop re , if no then process the req

requests will be processed at the fixed rate, so fixed rate processing

here queue act as bucket
fixed size queue we have here and accordingly req are processed


Params:
1.Queue/bucket size
2.Outflow rate

shopify uses this algo.

Pros:
-memory efficient
-fixed rate processing so it has stable outflow rate

cons:
-to parameters so hard to tune
-if there is a sale the queue can get quickly get filled


Fixed window counter algo **********

it has fixed window where requests are processed.

one major issue : The Edge of time window

Pros:
-Memory efficient
-easy to understand
-Resetting

Cons:
-EAt the dge of the window no requests are processed



Sliding Window Log Algo **********

here we log the time stamp of every request and this removes the fixed window edge of the window isse as well

Pros:
-very accurate

cons:
-consumes lot of memory cuz of logs


Now to fixed both the issues we faced in fix and sliding winoow we have another algo:



Sliding Window Counter Algo **********



Pros:
-memory efficient

cons:
-since we are rounding off and taking a certain %, its not very accurate





